{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/42550-world-of-darkness-map-maker","id":42550,"title":"World of Darkness map maker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T16:32:49-08:00","id":42550,"title":"World of Darkness map maker","content":"Do people use map making software for designing their WoD cities? I am looking for software which allows you to make a city with some districts without too much effort. Otherwise I stick to the old paper and pencil method. I can only find map making software for fantasy rpg's. They seems more geared towards either making world maps with mountains and lakes and such or making medieval cities with every building in that city on the map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:22:27-08:00","id":42578,"title":"","content":"I like using Google Maps to make mine. For example, here's one I'm working on for running my Chicago tabletop Requiem game. Some of the places shown are listed in the WoD Chicago book, with a couple of custom additions specific to my players, but you get the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Simply my opinion. Others may vary.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/892-theratt","name":"theratt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:28:32-08:00","id":42589,"title":"","content":"I use Google Maps as well. They even have a lot of old maps loaded now too, making it even more useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T02:07:53-08:00","id":42774,"title":"","content":"I like to use Google maps too - sometimes by taking an image from there and doodling in a few new details or alterations with Illustrator or Photoshop","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:31:56-08:00","id":42937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theratt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/42550-world-of-darkness-map-maker?p=42578#post42578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">